 until about 180 metres, when Woodring shot past him to win.  Edward might have run better had he not strained a muscle in the semi-finals."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Woodring was described in Barcs, as follows, “Allen, if he could avoid it, never spoke.  He lived a very unsportsmanlike life, and was one of the most studious and conscientious athletes.  Actually, he arrived in Antwerp by accident.  He was unable to win a place in the official selection contests and was included on the list only in the last minute.  He trained with great diligence.  So much so that his shoes fell apart, which was a major disaster. […] Woodring was unable to obtain any track shoes.  Finally, one of the other athletes loaned him his own ones, but only for the duration of the race.”"] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "247"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79212"} "Allen Woodring"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "22.8 (1 h9)"] [:td {} "22.1est / at 1 metre (2 h2)"] [:td {} "22.4 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "22.0 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "216"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78873"} "Charley Paddock"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "23.2 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "22.9est / chest behind (2 h3)"] [:td {} "22.5est / at ½ metre (2 h2)"] [:td {} "22.0est / at 10 cm (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}